{"c":[{"id":"3f04308e6f2b8a85","sum":"Accessibility quirks (Oct 2): Chrome titles in AXGroup and AXWebArea stay out of keys; Chrome rejects AXManualAccessibility; web DOM changes post no AX notification; background AppKit focus only in its key window; Gemma needs <bos> (BOSRuntime).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b99fccd1ca3e2300","sum":"Chrome: top AXGroup and AXWebArea carry window and page titles, so keep them out of element keys (E8). Chrome and Helium reject AXManualAccessibility (-25205) yet expose web AX; Electron accepts it. Web pages post no AX notification for DOM text changes (E1).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T100848Z-2317db88abe7ef57","text":"Chrome names its top AXGroup after the window title and AXWebArea after the page title; keep both out of element keys or every key moves on a title change (E8).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T100848Z-7a26e801e62c7446","text":"Chrome and Helium reject AXManualAccessibility (-25205) but still expose web AX; Electron apps accept it. Web pages post no AX notification for DOM text, insert or remove changes (E1).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"97fe10de523bdd37","sum":"A background AppKit app posts AX focus notifications only in its key window; fixtures makeKey() (no activation) before makeFirstResponder. KeyType tokenizes without <bos>; Gemma derails, so apps/caret wraps the runtime (BOSRuntime), not packages/.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T100848Z-bac1844f3b887c52","text":"A non-frontmost AppKit app posts AX focus notifications only inside its key window; fixtures call makeKey() (no activation) before makeFirstResponder.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T113723Z-0310b3f1df11a0ac","text":"KeyType tokenizes with add_special=false; Gemma GGUFs need <bos> or output derails. apps/caret wraps the runtime (BOSRuntime) instead of editing packages/.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c38b4998923b616f","sum":"Shared-Mac fixture lore: synthetic keys go to LaunchServices' front app and caret-fixture can take the foreground, so poll lsappinfo front; reader writes act only in --act-pids; fill recency uses the window left just before the form.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"205b1d0a36b8a24e","sum":"Shared-Mac input: synthetic HID keys go to LaunchServices' front app (guard on lsappinfo front); caret-screen write/press act only in --act-pids (subset of --only-pids), and rechecks fail closed on unreadable role/value/label.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T113723Z-250b757576dc3838","text":"Synthetic HID keys go to LaunchServices' front app, not the owner of the frontmost window; guard on lsappinfo front before typing into a fixture.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T114801Z-32531afb7e4fe1e0","text":"caret-screen write/press verbs act only in --act-pids, which must be a subset of --only-pids; without it the reader only reads. Rechecks fail closed on unreadable role/subrole/value/label.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"55197345bf228f3c","sum":"Fill recency uses the window left just before the form's last focus, not the latest focus (else Jev answers none). caret-fixture spawned from the frontmost app took the foreground; it now deactivates on activation; poll lsappinfo front in GUI runs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T114801Z-431742a743596ba6","text":"Fill recency: take the just-left window from focus history (the window before the form's last focus), not the latest focus; latest-focus made Jev answer none on most fields once the user moved to another form.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T130715Z-7922f91e68f9ff52","text":"caret-fixture spawned from the frontmost app (T3 or a terminal) became the active app and held the foreground for a whole run; it now deactivates on becoming active. Poll lsappinfo front during GUI runs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
